{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And Rachel died, and was buried on the way to Ephrath.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory darshaned: it is the dignity of women that their burial be in the place of their death. For Rachel died in Bethlehem and was buried in Bethlehem, and likewise we find with Sarah: ״ותמת שרה בקרית ארבע היא חברון״ — she died in Hebron and was buried in Hebron, as it says (Genesis 23:19): ״ואחרי כן קבר אברהם וגו׳,״ and likewise we find with Miriam, as it says (Numbers 20:1): ״ותמת שם מרים ותקבר שם.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:51.752569384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}